ng the operation.\n30:5. RANGE: list newer released versions whose sources you verified share the same mechanism. Include only versions you actually verified; when you cannot verify newer versions, record only 0.12.7.\n35:  \"summary\": \"one sentence naming the mechanism and why the image cannot perform it\",\n38:skipped_versions must include 0.12.7; reasons are published verbatim in index.json and the pull request, so write them for a reader who has not seen this analysis. Never base the verdict on a red test, a library's own error type, or its error message — only on the mechanism you traced in the library's source. Any uncertainty at any step means repairable: attempting the fix is the safe default, a wrong skip freezes versions that were never attempted.\n44:    \"title\": \"[Automation] native-image run fails for io.jsonwebtoken:jjwt-gson:0.12.7\",\n45:    \"label\": \"fails-native-image-run\",\n46:    \"body\": \"## native-image run on ubuntu-latest / JDK 25 / mode current-defaults\\n\\nFailure kind: native-image run\\nOS: ubuntu-latest\\nJDK: 25\\nNative-image mode: current-defaults\\nReproducer: `env GVM_TCK_LV=0.12.7 GVM_TCK_NATIVE_IMAGE_MODE=current-defaults ./gradlew clean test -Pcoordinates=io.jsonwebtoken:jjwt-gson:0.12.0`\\nRunner log: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/actions/runs/32316088693\\nLast 300 lines of the log (excerpt truncated to fit the GitHub issue size limit):\\n```console\\nmetadata/metadata/org.junit.platform/junit-platform-commons/1.8.2,/home/runner/work/graalvm-reachability-metadata/graalvm-reachability-metadata/metadata/org.junit.jupiter/junit-jupiter-params/5.9.2,/home/runner/work/graalvm-reachability-metadata/graalvm-reachability-metadata/metadata/org.junit.jupiter/junit-jupiter-engine/5.8.2,/home/runner/work/graalvm-reachability-metadata/graalvm-reachability-metadata/metadata/org.junit.platform/junit-platform-engine/1.10.4,/home/runner/work/graalvm-reachability-metadata/graalvm-reachability-metadata/metada