a. Preserved work: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fkimeta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-9337-fails-native-image-run-io.jsonwebtoken-jjwt-gson-0.12.7-0cf22873\n\nThe metadata repair itself succeeded: `logs/io.jsonwebtoken:jjwt-gson:0.12.7/native-image-run-fix/fixTestNativeImageRun-2026-10-07T02-05-54-427705Z.log` reports `BUILD SUCCESSFUL` and produced the `0.12.7` metadata checkpoint. The subsequent dynamic-access report failed because `build/native/nativeTestCompile/dynamic-access` was not generated. After falling back to test generation, all three iterations made only transient test edits and did not produce a verified result; metrics record 3 iterations, 0 generated LOC, and identical starting/ending commits.\n\nPlease inspect:\n- `logs/io.jsonwebtoken:jjwt-gson:0.12.7/dynamic-access-report/generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport-2026-10-07T02-09-47-375627Z.log`\n- `logs/io.jsonwebtoken:jjwt-gson:0.12.7/issue-requested-metadata/pi-generation-2026-10-07T02-13-10-838808Z.log`\n- `logs/io.jsonwebtoken:jjwt-gson:0.12.7/issue-requested-metadata/pi.log`\n\nManual next steps:\n1. Diagnose why the dynamic-access-enabled native build creates no `dynamic-access` output directory.\n2. Review and manually apply the proposed `Jjwt_gsonTest` coverage for the `Jwts.header()`, `Jwts.claims()`, `Jwts.builder()`, and `Jwts.parser()` supplier paths.\n3. Run the issue reproducer under both `current-defaults` and `future-defaults-all`, then validate the generated `0.12.7` metadata.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0b706362619398fc016ac5ab921e4887d08f9b44601c3df527\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 2119, "output": 970, "cacheRead": 187776, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 516, "totalTokens": 190865, "cost": {"input": 0.008476, "output": 0.0194, "cacheRead": 0.07511040000000001, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.1029864}}, "stopReason": "stop", "timestamp